## Future Invocation Contract

This command is documentation only. It was not executed:

```sh
node .tmp/resume182-6-n9-display-FIRST/run.mjs \
  --parent-ready STEMROBIN-182:182-6:n9-approved \
  --approved-choices /absolute/parent-approved/flat-choice-directory \
  --validation-receipt /absolute/parent-provided/validation.receipt.record \
  --text-evidence /absolute/parent-provided/n9-text-evidence.json \
  --answer-evidence /absolute/parent-provided/n9-answer-evidence.json \
  --choice-evidence /absolute/parent-provided/n9-choice-semantic-evidence.json
```

Exact argument order is required. All five paths must be absolute and resolve
inside the specified worktree; choice inputs must be outside this output root.
The marker is an invocation guard, NOT authorization. The parent must separately
authorize the exact final choice directory/receipt/evidence paths after all
content gates pass. No paths or approved hashes have been invented here.

The choice directory must contain seed.json, draft.json, review.json, plus the
spec/output/review/render-or-generation records needed by referenced candidates.
Existing canonical seed/draft review bindings and the seed's current lesson,
exercise and figure trace hashes are checked; the prior validator is not rerun.
Content evidence is parent-provided JSON with pass verdict/outcome/status, or an
exitCode/returncode 0 when no verdict is declared. An explicitly declared lesson
must be N9. These records are fingerprinted, not new mathematical approvals.

Current content was observed as 17 prose blocks, 16 written exercises (109-124),
and no original figures. Counts of choice questions, options and candidates are
derived only from the future approved draft. No current seed was approved by
this preparation.

## Reuse and Boundaries

Implementation structure was copied from the existing
`.tmp/resume182-4-postaccount/n13-display-FIRST/run.mjs`, not its evidence files.
Reused helpers: sha/canonical/norm/same, own/save/event/check/fingerprint/under/
stage, projection/writtenText, installDisplayTools/pageSafety, unionArea and
captureCoverage; renderOnce and cleanup were narrowly adapted.
proseFlow/proseOutline/sectionBreakIndices remain from existing htmlfrag.js;
choice table projection still uses existing marked. No new renderer, framework,
metric schema, mechanical-defence run, or general checking system was introduced.
N13-specific table/hash/approval/math-fragment/recovery/screenshot reuse branches
were removed. Neither N13 nor N22 was run; no evidence package was copied.

Parent supplied the ignored app/node_modules, .agents/skills/node_modules and
lesson node_modules symlinks. The runner uses normal worktree resolution to those
existing dependencies; this preparation installed, copied or linked none.

Future renderer: `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/tools/render_lesson.js`, one child
invocation only. Stage root: `runtime-FIRST/scratch/7a/`; only this lesson,
approved seed/draft/review and actually referenced candidate assets are staged.
Only scratch candidate paths change; approved files remain read-only, candidate
bytes bind to draft hashes, and input hashes are rechecked during cleanup.
`approved-choice-view.json` exports the current approved views, counts, figure
inventory and raw seed/draft/review hashes; it is not served.
No book-wide content, answers, N13 table or prior screenshots are staged.

Future browser is isolated headless Chromium, two fresh contexts with native
1440x960 and 390x844 viewports, each visiting text/exercises/choices (six pages).
Only the loopback HTML allowlist is served; local inline fonts/assets, CSP,
request/WebSocket blocking, console/page/network failures remain enforced.
Actual Range/HTML/SVG geometry, full mathematical visual DOM and text projection,
actual media widths and SVG label sizes >=16px, edge reachability and native
scroll-window coverage remain in the existing helper path. Text Range bounds use
0.5px allowance; figures/SVG/math rules use zero containment allowance.
Screenshots are native viewport, unresized/uncropped, unobserved; no image is
opened by the runner.

First failure stops dependent work, retains generated files and writes
failure-receipt.record plus report/usage/visual handoff when the owned filesystem
remains writable. Child/context/browser/server cleanup is in finally; no retry
or renderer-recovery mode exists. An existing runtime-FIRST directory stops a
second invocation without overwriting its evidence.
Runtime success means only RUNTIME_PASS_VISUAL_PENDING, never content/visual/
application approval.

## Preparation Tool Faults

1. Read-only dependency/output lookup (`ls -ld`) exited 1 before the parent's
   dependency update: app/node_modules, .agents/skills/node_modules and the new
   output directory did not yet exist. Lesson dependencies already had a symlink.
   The parent subsequently supplied app/agents symlinks; a later read-only lookup
   confirmed all three. Only the authorized output directory was created here.
   No renderer or browser was started to diagnose this lookup.
2. Read-only `rg` lookup exited 2 because guessed image-spec reference filenames
   `references/spec-schema.md` and `references/spec.md` did not exist. Existing
   SKILL.md matches were returned. No files were created there and no image was
   opened. This was a documentation-path lookup fault, not runtime evidence.

